## The Petite Standard

The Petite Standard describes what makes a rose gold setting proven for emerald cut diamonds — and why the [Petite Solitaire](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/petite-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-item-195429?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is the benchmark.

The Petite Solitaire in 14k Rose Gold has accumulated **1,186 reviews** — the highest review count of any rose gold engagement ring setting. That is a reliable signal. 1,186 buyers have purchased this setting, received the ring, and chosen to rate it.

Settings that don't fit a wide range of stone shapes don't accumulate that volume of satisfied reviews. The Petite Solitaire's thin, clean band and four-prong head work with virtually every fancy shape including the emerald cut — the head allows the step-cut table to sit high and visible, the thin band doesn't compete with the stone's width.

The Petite Standard is the baseline test for any rose gold setting: does the setting's head accommodate a rectangular step-cut stone? Does the band's width and design style complement rather than compete with the emerald cut's clean geometric outline? A setting that passes both checks is likely to look excellent with an emerald cut in rose gold.

The 18 settings in this guide all pass this test — some clearly, some with caveats noted.

