## Solitaire Settings in Rose Gold: $935 to $1,650

Solitaires are the most popular style for emerald cut diamonds in rose gold. The plain band lets the step-cut stone dominate. The rose gold color provides warmth without adding visual complexity that competes with the stone's architecture.

[![Emerald cut diamond rose gold ring classic solitaire setting](/images/emerald-cut-diamond-rose-gold-ring-classic-solitaire.avif)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?styleIDs=all&MetalType=rg&ShapeID=Emerald&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

**Classic Comfort Fit Solitaire in 14k Rose Gold (2.5mm) — [$935](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/classic-comfort-fit-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-25mm-item-203282?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** (232 reviews)

The most affordable rose gold solitaire. Comfort fit means the interior of the band is rounded for all-day wearability. 232 reviews confirms this is a proven design.

The 2.5mm band width is appropriate for emerald cut diamonds at 1ct+ — narrow enough to not compete with the stone's face-up width.

**Petite Solitaire in 14k Rose Gold — [$1,000](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/petite-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-item-195429?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** (1,186 reviews)

The benchmark setting. 1,186 reviews makes this the most review-validated rose gold engagement ring setting in the market. The thin petite band and four-prong head let the emerald cut stone sit clean and visible.

If you're unsure which setting to choose, start here — The Petite Standard is built on this ring.

[![Emerald cut diamond rose gold ring petite solitaire setting](/images/emerald-cut-diamond-rose-gold-ring-petite-solitaire.avif)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?styleIDs=all&MetalType=rg&ShapeID=Emerald&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

**Classic Simple Solitaire in 14k Rose Gold — [$1,145](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/classic-simple-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-item-203345?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** (284 reviews)

Slightly heavier shank than the Petite at a moderate price. The "simple" design has no embellishment — pure metal, four prongs, the stone. 284 reviews.

For buyers who want a little more band weight than the Petite without adding pavé diamonds.

**Tapered Cathedral Solitaire in 14k Rose Gold — [$1,240](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/tapered-cathedral-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-item-203285?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** (254 reviews)

The cathedral arch under the setting head elevates the emerald cut stone higher above the band. This is a deliberate visual choice — the elevated stone looks more prominent. 254 reviews.

The tapered shank narrows toward the head, which works well with the emerald cut's wider face-up outline.

[![Emerald cut diamond rose gold ring cathedral solitaire](/images/emerald-cut-diamond-rose-gold-ring-cathedral-solitaire.avif)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?styleIDs=all&MetalType=rg&ShapeID=Emerald&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

**Engraved Solitaire in 14k Rose Gold by James Allen — [$1,365](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/engraved-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-by-james-allen-item-314957?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** (80 reviews)

Engraved detailing on the band adds texture without adding diamond weight. The engraving creates a vintage-adjacent character that complements rose gold's romantic aesthetic. Pairs well with the emerald cut's step-cut geometry — the engraved band provides visual interest without competing with the stone's architecture.

**Classic Tapered Solitaire in 14k Rose Gold — [$1,500](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/classic-tapered-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-item-203259?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** (180 reviews)

Heavier shank that tapers toward the stone head. 180 reviews on a mid-range priced solitaire confirms solid buyer satisfaction. The tapered design frames the stone with increasing band width toward the finger sides — a more substantial look than the Petite or Simple without adding pavé.

**Criss Cross Solitaire in 14k Rose Gold by James Allen — [$1,650](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/criss-cross-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-by-james-allen-item-311129?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** (20 reviews)

Two bands cross under the center stone before meeting at the sides. This design creates a distinctive shadow pattern beneath the step-cut stone. Works well for buyers who want a solitaire look with more design interest than a plain band.

