## Best For

**Budget buyers:** The [Classic Comfort Fit Solitaire at $935](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/classic-comfort-fit-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-25mm-item-203282?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) plus a [lab 1ct IGI emerald cut](https://www.bluenile.com/lab-grown-diamond-search?shape=emerald&caratMin=0.9&caratMax=1.1&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) totals around $1,430. Apply The H-Color Discount — go H-color on any natural stone to save another $500+ vs. G.

**Buyers wanting proven results:** The [Petite Solitaire at $1,000 with 1,186 reviews](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/petite-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-item-195429?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is The Petite Standard. Pair with a [1ct GIA H-VS2 natural emerald cut](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?shape=emerald&caratMin=0.9&caratMax=1.1&colorMin=H&colorMax=H&clarityMin=VS2&clarityMax=VS2&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) for approximately $3,500 total.

**Buyers wanting sparkle on the band:** The [Riviera Pavé Lab-Grown at $1,250 with 479 reviews](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/riviera-pave-lab-grown-diamond-engagement-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-1-6-ct-tw-item-309312?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is the highest-value pavé option. For maximum halo presence, the [Falling Edge Pavé Halo at $2,470 with 369 reviews](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/falling-edge-pave-diamond-halo-engagement-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-by-james-allen-item-311111?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is the most validated option in this category.

**Buyers deciding between rose gold and white gold:** Apply the Warm Contrast Rule — rose gold creates contrast with the step-cut table, white gold blends with it. Apply the H-Color Discount — rose gold saves 15–25% on stone cost with identical appearance. If you want warmth, rose gold wins. If you want the icy, colorless look, go white gold. The stone's proportion standards are identical in either metal.

